      "text": "- We can apply the formula $(a - b)(a + b) = a^2 - b^2$ to simplify $(10x + 2)(10x + 6) = 100x^2 + 60x + 4 = 4(25x^2 + 15x + 1)$.\n- Therefore, $(10x + 2)(10x + 6)(5x + 5) = (25x^2 + 15x + 1)(5x + 5) = 25x(10x + 6) + (10x^2 + 4x + 1)$.\n- Finally, using the formula for the difference of squares, we get $(25x^2+106x+5)(10x+6)=25x(10x+6) + (10x^2 + 4x + 1)$.\n- Recognizing that $(5x + 5) = 5(x + 1)$, we substitute to obtain $25x(5(x + 1)) + (10x^2 + 4x + 1)$.\n- Therefore, $5x(25x^2 + 15x + 1)$ which is divisible by $5^2 = 25$. Thus, the largest integer that always divides the expression is \\boxed{25}.",
